=== absolute cost ladder, best of 21 rounds of 2000 dispatches (E1) ===
phi(K) = t(2K)/t(K).  A threadgroup-doubling change pays only if phi < 2.
t/K is the per-threadgroup cost: flat means work-limited, falling means
the added threadgroups are absorbed by idle cores.
